    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0476" n="380" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg380"/>

                <head>No. 195.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Hegermann.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 7th of
                    January last, I have the honor to inclose herewith, for your information, a copy
                    of a dispatch of <pb facs="0477" n="381" xml:id="pg381"/> the 9th of February,
                    1874, No. 19,<anchor n="*" xml:id="d197-f1"/> and of its accompaniments, from
                    Mr. Williams, chargé d’affaires, <hi rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi>, of the
                    United States at Peking, relating to the protest made by the Chinese authorities
                    against the action of the Great Northern Telegraph Company in that country.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="*" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>For this correspondence, see under “China.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
